{
  "version": "Notebook/1.0",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "# 🚨 WUfB - KB Early Warning Dashboard\n\nDaily **success/failure rate trend per KB**, so a worsening quality update can be spotted in the days following its release, before it becomes a widespread compliance problem.\n\n**Chart**: one line per `TargetKBNumber` (`FailureRatePercent` by `Day`), plus a flat red **Alert Threshold** reference line at a configurable %. Any KB whose line crosses above the threshold is a candidate for a rollback/pause decision.\n\n**Source**: `UCClientUpdateStatus`, filtered on `UpdateCategory == \"WindowsQualityUpdate\"`. `Failed` counts `ClientState` in `OnHold`/`Canceled` (safeguard hold, deferral, or canceled offering).\n\n> Standalone version of this query: `kql/10-early-warning-kb-trend.kql`."
      },
      "name": "text-header"
    },
    {
      "type": 9,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "id": "b1a1e001-1111-4a1a-b1c1-111111111111",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "TimeRange",
            "type": 4,
            "isRequired": true,
            "typeSettings": {
              "selectableValues": [
                {
                  "durationMs": 604800000
                },
                {
                  "durationMs": 1209600000
                },
                {
                  "durationMs": 2592000000
                },
                {
                  "durationMs": 7776000000
                }
              ],
              "allowCustom": true
            },
            "value": {
              "durationMs": 2592000000
            },
            "label": "Time Range"
          },
          {
            "id": "b1a1e001-2222-4a1a-b1c1-222222222222",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "TargetKBFilter",
            "type": 2,
            "isRequired": true,
            "multiSelect": true,
            "quote": "'",
            "delimiter": ",",
            "query": "UCClientUpdateStatus\n| where TimeGenerated {TimeRange}\n| where UpdateCategory == \"WindowsQualityUpdate\"\n| where isnotempty(TargetKBNumber)\n| distinct TargetKBNumber\n| sort by TargetKBNumber desc\n| project value = TargetKBNumber, label = TargetKBNumber",
            "typeSettings": {
              "additionalResourceOptions": [
                "value::all"
              ],
              "selectAllValue": "*"
            },
            "defaultValue": "value::all",
            "queryType": 0,
            "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
            "label": "KB Number"
          },
          {
            "id": "b1a1e001-3333-4a1a-b1c1-333333333333",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "FailureThreshold",
            "type": 1,
            "isRequired": true,
            "value": 15,
            "label": "Failure Rate Alert Threshold (%)"
          }
        ],
        "style": "pills",
        "queryType": 0,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces"
      },
      "name": "parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "let _threshold = toreal({FailureThreshold});\nlet _kb = dynamic([{TargetKBFilter}]);\nlet _kbTrend = UCClientUpdateStatus\n    | where TimeGenerated {TimeRange}\n    | where UpdateCategory == \"WindowsQualityUpdate\"\n    | where \"*\" in (_kb) or TargetKBNumber in (_kb)\n    | summarize arg_max(TimeGenerated, ClientState) by AzureADDeviceId, TargetKBNumber, bin(TimeGenerated, 1d)\n    | summarize\n        Installed = countif(ClientState == \"Installed\"),\n        Failed = countif(ClientState in (\"OnHold\", \"Canceled\")),\n        Total = count()\n        by Day = bin(TimeGenerated, 1d), TargetKBNumber\n    | extend FailureRatePercent = round(100.0 * Failed / Total, 1)\n    | project Day, TargetKBNumber, FailureRatePercent;\nlet _days = _kbTrend | distinct Day;\nlet _thresholdLine = _days\n    | extend TargetKBNumber = \"⚠ Alert Threshold\", FailureRatePercent = _threshold\n    | project Day, TargetKBNumber, FailureRatePercent;\n_kbTrend\n| union _thresholdLine\n| sort by TargetKBNumber asc, Day asc",
        "size": 0,
        "title": "Daily Failure Rate % by KB (with alert threshold)",
        "timeContext": {
          "durationMs": 0
        },
        "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange",
        "queryType": 0,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
        "visualization": "linechart",
        "chartSettings": {
          "xAxis": "Day",
          "yAxis": [
            "FailureRatePercent"
          ],
          "group": "TargetKBNumber",
          "createOtherGroup": 0,
          "seriesLabelSettings": [
            {
              "seriesName": "⚠ Alert Threshold",
              "color": "redBright"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "name": "chart-kb-failure-rate-trend"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## 📋 Days Above Threshold\n\nOnly the KB/Day combinations where `FailureRatePercent` exceeds the configured threshold — the actionable early-warning list."
      },
      "name": "text-detail-header"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "let _threshold = toreal({FailureThreshold});\nlet _kb = dynamic([{TargetKBFilter}]);\nUCClientUpdateStatus\n| where TimeGenerated {TimeRange}\n| where UpdateCategory == \"WindowsQualityUpdate\"\n| where \"*\" in (_kb) or TargetKBNumber in (_kb)\n| summarize arg_max(TimeGenerated, ClientState) by AzureADDeviceId, TargetKBNumber, bin(TimeGenerated, 1d)\n| summarize\n    Installed = countif(ClientState == \"Installed\"),\n    Failed = countif(ClientState in (\"OnHold\", \"Canceled\")),\n    Installing = countif(ClientState == \"Installing\"),\n    Total = count()\n    by Day = bin(TimeGenerated, 1d), TargetKBNumber\n| extend\n    SuccessRatePercent = round(100.0 * Installed / Total, 1),\n    FailureRatePercent = round(100.0 * Failed / Total, 1)\n| where FailureRatePercent > _threshold\n| extend Status = \"Above Threshold\"\n| project Day, TargetKBNumber, Total, Installed, Failed, Installing, SuccessRatePercent, FailureRatePercent, Status\n| sort by Day desc, FailureRatePercent desc",
        "size": 0,
        "title": "KB/Day above the Failure Rate Alert Threshold",
        "timeContext": {
          "durationMs": 0
        },
        "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange",
        "queryType": 0,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
        "visualization": "table",
        "gridSettings": {
          "formatters": [
            {
              "columnMatch": "FailureRatePercent",
              "formatter": 8,
              "formatOptions": {
                "min": 0,
                "max": 100,
                "palette": "greenRed"
              }
            },
            {
              "columnMatch": "SuccessRatePercent",
              "formatter": 8,
              "formatOptions": {
                "min": 0,
                "max": 100,
                "palette": "redGreen"
              }
            },
            {
              "columnMatch": "Status",
              "formatter": 18,
              "formatOptions": {
                "thresholdsOptions": "icons",
                "thresholdsGrid": [
                  {
                    "operator": "==",
                    "thresholdValue": "Above Threshold",
                    "representation": "3",
                    "text": "{0}{1}"
                  },
                  {
                    "operator": "Default",
                    "representation": "unknown",
                    "text": "{0}{1}"
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "filter": true,
          "sortBy": [
            {
              "itemKey": "Day",
              "sortOrder": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "name": "grid-kb-above-threshold"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "---\n### Notes\n- **Failed**: `ClientState` in `OnHold` (safeguard hold, deferral, pause) or `Canceled` (offering canceled). Not the same as a hard installation error, but it does represent devices that did not successfully complete the KB rollout.\n- **Failure Rate Alert Threshold**: adjust the `FailureThreshold` parameter (default 15%) to match your risk tolerance; it drives both the red reference line on the chart and the filtered detail table below.\n- The chart groups by `TargetKBNumber`, so a newly released KB with a rising red-crossing line is the visual early-warning signal; the table gives the exact day/KB list for follow-up (e.g., pausing the rollout via Windows Update rings, or opening a support case for a specific KB).\n- For automated proactive alerting (instead of a dashboard to check manually), see `kql/13-alert-do-efficiency-drop.kql` and `kql/14-alert-new-error-codes.kql` for the Scheduled Query Rule pattern; the same pattern can be applied to this `FailureRatePercent > threshold` condition."
      },
      "name": "text-footer"
    }
  ],
  "fallbackResourceIds": [],
  "$schema": "https://github.com/Microsoft/Application-Insights-Workbooks/blob/master/schema/workbook.json",
  "styleSettings": {},
  "fromTemplateId": "custom-wufb-kb-early-warning-dashboard"
}
